# LSan (LeakSanitizer) suppressions for lazy-image NAPI stress tests
#
# V8 and Node.js intentionally retain certain heap objects (inline caches,
# feedback vectors, descriptor arrays, etc.) for the lifetime of the
# process rather than freeing them at exit.  These appear as "leaks" to
# LSan but are expected behaviour, not bugs in lazy-image.
#
# Patterns here suppress only V8/Node.js internal allocations so that
# genuine Rust-side leaks are still caught and reported.

# --- V8 internals -----------------------------------------------------------
leak:v8::internal::

# --- V8 builtins (JIT stubs, IC handlers) -----------------------------------
leak:Builtins_

# --- Node.js runtime --------------------------------------------------------
leak:node::
